course: dictionary
lesson: 420
title: Approval: thinking well of something
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Approval is a noun with two meanings. The first is thinking that someone or something is good or right, so you like it. The second is official permission or agreement to do something. The context tells you which meaning you need.
explain: «All Nature joining in a chorus of approval to the song of self-praise that his own heart was singing to him...» The trees and birds seem to agree that he is wonderful. So approval means liking or thinking well of something. Ask yourself: is someone giving a good opinion, or saying yes officially?
explain: Look for clues. «Vaccines are tested in the lab and then in trials with thousands of people before approval» shows that approval is official permission, given after tests. A school trip needs parents' approval, which is the official yes on a permission slip.
fact: Approval means thinking that someone or something is good or right.
fact: Approval can also mean official permission to do something.
fact: «Win approval» means to get people to agree with or like what you do.
fact: «Nod of approval» means a small nod that shows you think something is good.
fact: Approval is usually uncountable, so you say «approval» and not «an approval» for a feeling; a single official permission can be called «an approval».
exercise: «The teacher gave a nod of approval when Mia finished her drawing.» What does the nod show? | She needed more paper | *She liked the drawing and thought it was good | She was going to be late | She was angry and wanted her to stop
exercise: Ella's plan for a school garden needs the teacher's approval before it can start. What does approval mean here? | A feeling of being sad | Something easy to pick up | *Official permission to go ahead | A small garden tool
exercise: «Vaccines are tested in the lab and then in trials with thousands of people before approval.» What comes before approval? | A party for the scientists | *Tests in the lab and trials with people | A new name for the vaccine | Nothing, approval comes first
test: A shop says «The jacket is yours on approval.» What does on approval mean? | It is for a sale in the summer | You must wear it outside | *You may return it if you do not like it | It is free to keep forever
test: Which phrase means that people have liked and agreed with something? | *Win approval | Lose approval | Approval tickets | Turn off approval
exam: Which sentence uses approval to mean official permission? | Her approval of the cake was shown by a big smile | Mum looked at the painting with approval | The crowd gave a cheer of approval at the goal | *The council gave approval for the new playground
